12. On the basis of the discussions made hereinabove, I pass the following;
ORDER i) The appeal preferred by the Insurance Company of the Car is allowed-in-part;
ii) The appeal preferred by the claimants is dismissed;
 iii) The judgment and award dated 14.10.2019 passed  by Additional Senior Civil Judge MACT,
Srirangapatna in MVC.No.1021/2017 is modified;
 iv) The claimants are entitled to a sum of M/S National Insurance Company Ltd vs Mrs Sumangala on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/4174715/
7  Rs.31,70,000/-;
 - 14 -  NC: 2024:KHC:14598  v) The interest awarded by the tribunal at 9% p.a is  reduced to 6% p.a;
 vi) The amount in deposit before this Court made by  the respective Insurance Company shall be transmitted to the jurisdictional tribunal forthwith;
vii) The excess amount if any shall be returned and refunded to the respective Insurance Company;
viii) Balance compensation amount shall be deposited before the jurisdictional tribunal forthwith;
ix) The interest component of excess amount if any deposited shall be refunded to the appellant- Insurance company of the Ertiga car;
x) On deposit of balance amount based on the reduced interest as ordered by this Court today, the MACT shall refund the excess amount paid by respondent Nos.2 and 4-Insurance companies, if any.

